{
  "_comment": "Golden vectors for ARCHITECTURE Section7.1 clock offset estimation, core.sync / RideLinkCore.Sync. rtt_us = (t4-t1)-(t3-t2); offset_us = ((t2-t1)+(t3-t4))/2 (integer division truncating toward zero). Outlier rule: discard any sample whose rtt exceeds 2x the window's minimum rtt. The retained minimum-RTT sample's offset is the window's raw estimate; jitter_us = (max_rtt-min_rtt)/2 among retained samples. Smoothing: EWMA alpha=0.2 applied as exact-rational integer arithmetic (delta * 2 / 10, truncating toward zero) rather than floating point, so both platforms produce byte-identical integers. Step-reject rule: a candidate offset differing from the previous accepted offset by more than 30000us (30ms) is rejected and remembered as a pending candidate rather than applied; it is applied (with EWMA smoothing) only if a later window's candidate agrees with the pending one within 10000us (10ms) -- the confirmation tolerance is an implementation parameter of this pure estimator (not a wire value), chosen and pinned by these vectors so both platforms use one number.",
  "algorithm": {
    "rtt_us": "(t4 - t1) - (t3 - t2)",
    "offset_us": "((t2 - t1) + (t3 - t4)) / 2, integer division truncating toward zero",
    "outlier_rule": "keep samples with rtt_us <= 2 * min(rtt_us) in the window",
    "best_sample": "the kept sample with the smallest rtt_us; first occurrence wins ties",
    "jitter_us": "(max(kept rtt_us) - min(kept rtt_us)) / 2, integer division truncating toward zero",
    "ewma_alpha": "0.2, applied as previous + (candidate - previous) * 2 / 10 with integer division truncating toward zero",
    "step_reject_threshold_us": 30000,
    "step_confirm_tolerance_us": 10000
  },
